<div class="wrap">

<h1>Eight Healthcare Sectors Suffolk Can Name and Claim</h1>
<p class="lede">Suffolk educates students for healthcare careers across all three schools, but we have never had a shared way to say so. Our descriptions tend to list a few familiar programs and then trail off into "and more." That phrasing costs us something every time we use it. It makes genuine breadth sound accidental, it gives faculty, advisors, and employer partners no common vocabulary, and it leaves students in business, law, policy, and analytics with no reason to believe healthcare is a field open to them.</p>
<p class="lede">These eight sectors come from where Suffolk graduates actually work. Four describe types of organizations and four describe types of work that cut across them, because a radiation dosimetrist and a hospital finance analyst may share an employer without sharing a career. Named together, they turn a long list of programs into a map that a student can navigate, an employer can locate themselves on, and the University can stand behind.</p>

<div class="btngrid">
  <a class="btn" href="#s1" style="--c:#15284B;--fg:#fff">Hospital and Health System Leadership</a>
  <a class="btn" href="#s2" style="--c:#3CB4E5;--fg:#15284B">Behavioral and Mental Health</a>
  <a class="btn" href="#s3" style="--c:#40C1AC;--fg:#15284B">Radiation Oncology and Medical Imaging</a>
  <a class="btn" href="#s4" style="--c:#E7AB2A;--fg:#15284B">Life Sciences and Biotech</a>
  <a class="btn" href="#s5" style="--c:#CE3062;--fg:#fff">Public Health, Policy, and Community Care</a>
  <a class="btn" href="#s6" style="--c:#15284B;--fg:#fff">Health Law and Compliance</a>
  <a class="btn" href="#s7" style="--c:#3CB4E5;--fg:#15284B">Digital Health and Analytics</a>
  <a class="btn" href="#s8" style="--c:#40C1AC;--fg:#15284B">Healthcare Finance and Revenue</a>
</div>

<!-- ============== 1 ============== -->
<div class="sector" id="s1" style="border-top-color:#15284B">
  <h2>Hospital and Health System Leadership</h2>
  <p class="tagline">Running the institutions: operations, administration, program management, and department leadership.</p>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="blk"><h3>Programs</h3>
      <ul><li>Healthcare Administration, MHA</li><li>Healthcare Administration, three-year applied BS</li><li>Business Administration, MBA and Executive MBA</li><li>Business Analytics, MSBA</li><li>Biology, Psychology, Sociology at the entry level</li></ul></div>
    <div class="blk"><h3>Where graduates work</h3>
      <p class="emp">Massachusetts General Hospital &middot; Brigham and Women's Hospital &middot; Beth Israel Lahey Health &middot; Dana-Farber Cancer Institute &middot; Boston Children's Hospital &middot; Mass General Brigham &middot; Boston Medical Center &middot; Tufts Medicine &middot; Newton-Wellesley Hospital &middot; Cambridge Health Alliance &middot; Mass Eye and Ear &middot; Spaulding Rehabilitation</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="blk"><h3>Roles Suffolk graduates hold</h3>
    <ul class="roles">
      <li><b>Senior Research Project Manager</b><span>Dana-Farber Cancer Institute &middot; MHA</span></li>
      <li><b>Administrative Program Manager</b><span>Massachusetts General Hospital &middot; MBA</span></li>
      <li><b>Ambulatory Clinic Supervisor</b><span>Boston Children's Hospital &middot; MHA</span></li>
      <li><b>Operations Manager</b><span>Boston Medical Center &middot; MHA</span></li>
      <li><b>Senior Project Coordinator</b><span>Mass General Brigham &middot; MBA</span></li>
      <li><b>Lead Practice and OR Operations</b><span>Brigham and Women's Hospital &middot; MHA</span></li>
      <li><b>Department Coordinator</b><span>Newton-Wellesley Hospital &middot; MHA</span></li>
      <li><b>Practice Manager</b><span>Wellesley Dermatology Care &middot; MBA</span></li>
    </ul></div>
  <div class="star"><p><strong>Chimwemwe Clarke</strong>, MHA, is Nursing Director at Massachusetts General Hospital. <strong>Anu Gupte</strong>, MHA '17, is Program Director in the Innovator Growth Division at Mass General Brigham Innovation. Both return to campus to speak with students.</p></div>
</div>

<!-- ============== 2 ============== -->
