  <p class="tagline">Planning and delivering radiation treatment, and the imaging that guides it.</p>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="blk"><h3>Programs</h3>
      <ul><li>Medical Dosimetry, MS</li><li>Radiation Therapy, BS</li><li>Radiation Science, BS</li></ul></div>
    <div class="blk"><h3>Where graduates work</h3>
      <p class="emp">Massachusetts General Hospital &middot; Brigham and Women's Hospital &middot; Beth Israel Lahey Health &middot; Dana-Farber Cancer Institute &middot; Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center &middot; City of Hope &middot; Penn Medicine &middot; Yale New Haven Health &middot; UC San Diego Health &middot; University of Vermont Health Network &middot; Cooper University Health Care &middot; University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="unique"><p><strong>Suffolk's most distinctive claim in healthcare.</strong> Medical dosimetry is offered by only a handful of universities nationally. Suffolk graduates hold credentialed positions at NCI-designated cancer centers from Boston to San Diego, and the credential travels anywhere in the country.</p></div>
  <div class="blk" style="margin-top:14px"><h3>Roles Suffolk graduates hold</h3>
    <ul class="roles">
      <li><b>Certified Medical Dosimetrist</b><span>Brigham and Women's Hospital</span></li>
      <li><b>Medical Dosimetrist</b><span>Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center</span></li>
      <li><b>Radiation Therapist</b><span>Massachusetts General Hospital</span></li>
      <li><b>Medical Radiation Dosimetrist</b><span>University of Illinois Chicago Health</span></li>
      <li><b>Registered MRI Technologist</b><span>Tufts Medical Center</span></li>
      <li><b>Radiology Assistant</b><span>Mass General Brigham &middot; Biology</span></li>
    </ul></div>
  <div class="star"><p><strong>Jennifer Nguyen</strong>, MS Medical Dosimetry '22, is a Certified Medical Dosimetrist at Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center.</p></div>
</div>

<!-- ============== 4 ============== -->
